--- README.md (9125) ---
# LOGDRUM v2 — the amapiano log drum instrument

**UI: 100% Rust egui (eframe). DSP: 100% Rust. No React, no JavaScript UI, no JavaScript synthesis.**
The browser preview is the *same* egui instrument compiled to WebAssembly; the only JS in the product is
the generated wasm-bindgen loader glue and a ~60-line AudioWorklet driver that instantiates the Rust DSP
module and copies 128-sample blocks.

```
rust/
  core/     logdrum-core — synth engine + 204 factory presets + raw C ABI for AudioWorklet
  app/      logdrum-app  — egui/eframe instrument (wasm + native window), Web MIDI, groove player
  plugin/   nih-plug wrapper — CLAP + VST3 + standalone (older egui panel, see "Status")
  wasm/     optional wasm-bindgen wrapper around the core
web/        generated wasm-bindgen glue + gzip/base64 of the app wasm (no UI code)
index.html  canvas shell only
```

## Run

```bash
npm run build        # -> dist/index.html  (single file, boots egui, no network needed)
# or the dev server
npx vite
```

To rebuild the Rust/wasm assets after editing Rust or presets:

```bash
node scripts/gen-rust-presets.mjs   # data/presets.json -> rust/core/src/presets.rs
node scripts/build-wasm.mjs         # cargo

